diff --git a/docs/webhooks.md b/docs/webhooks.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..39b7737
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/webhooks.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Board webhooks
+
+Admins can add receivers from a board's existing Webhooks settings and choose
+which actions they receive. Only active webhooks subscribed to the action on
+that board receive an event. Rolled-back events do not produce deliveries.
+
+Generic receivers get the existing event JSON representation, including the
+card or comment, board, creator, and tenant-prefixed links. Slack receivers get
+`text`; Campfire and Basecamp chat receivers get HTML `content`.
+
+## Requests and delivery semantics
+
+Requests are JSON POSTs with these headers:
+
+- `X-Webhook-Id`: the stable delivery ID.
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: the UTC request timestamp.
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: the hexadecimal SHA-256 HMAC of the exact request body,
+  using the signing secret shown in settings.
+
+There is one delivery record per event/receiver pair. An atomic pending-to-in-
+progress claim prevents duplicate or concurrent jobs from issuing another POST.
+There are no HTTP retries or redirects, including after a timeout or worker
+crash. Receivers can use the delivery ID for deduplication.
+
+This guarantees at most one POST attempt, not exactly-once processing by an
+arbitrary remote server: a lost connection can leave it unknown whether the
+receiver processed the request. Exactly-once processing requires cooperation
+from the receiver (idempotent handling of the delivery ID).
+
+Receivers must resolve to a public IP. The connection is pinned to that address
+while preserving the hostname for HTTP and TLS. Connect/read/write timeouts are
+five seconds, with a fifteen-second overall HTTP deadline. Response bodies are
+limited to 16 KiB for logging.
+
+## Results and automatic shutoff
+
+The delivery log records request metadata, HTTP status, response headers/body,
+and transport errors. The board settings show the state, HTTP status, or error;
+the existing deliveries API exposes a summary without the signing header.
+Only 2xx responses count as successful.
+
+A receiver is switched off after at least ten consecutive failed deliveries
+spanning at least one hour. A successful delivery resets the streak. Reactivate
+from settings to reset the streak and receive future events. Already-queued
+deliveries will not send while the receiver is inactive.
+
+Delivery logs older than seven days are removed by the existing recurring
+cleanup task, which runs every fifteen minutes.
+
+## Regression tests
+
+Run the end-to-end reproduction and focused tests with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails test test/models/event/webhook_test.rb test/models/webhook_test.rb test/models/webhook
+```
